"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Location: only when you turn it on, to show you where you are on the map, what is near you and the route to a place, to check that you are at the places you mark as visited and, in the “Travel Pass”, to read you each stop as you arrive, for the treasure hunt and for “What am I looking at?”. It is not stored on any server. If you ask for a driving route, the start and end coordinates are sent to the routing service to work it out.";
